Subject: Record branch bias

What this does
  Counts, for every conditional branch, how many times it executed and how many
  of those took the branch target, and dumps them as a `B` line.

Why we need it
  The compiler lays out hot and cold blocks and needs to know which arm of each
  branch is hot. The profile recorded nothing about it.

What it adds
  `JSAotProfFunc.br_taken`/`br_total`, a static conditional-branch opcode table
  and the `B` line; `profmerge.py` sums the pair across sessions.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.

